PROVEX patch 08-fix-cal-anomaly-loss-zero-division
FIX, labelled separately: cal_anomaly_loss() divides by zero when no edge of a window exceeds mean + 1.5*std. Such a window now gets an average anomalous loss of 0 instead of crashing the queue construction; windows that work upstream are unaffected.
Series: upstream ProvenanceAnalytics/kairos@0e0b633beb46a1117c0a6d63be5d2481b59ac0dc DARPA/CADETS_E3, patches 01..11 applied in numeric order.
Paths are relative to DARPA/CADETS_E3: apply to a copy of kairos/upstream/ that is outside any git work tree (git apply <patch>), or from the repository root with git apply --directory=<copy dir> <patch>.

